    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW264xQ1rraVxBDBip6TeNyfG)_\n\n## Changes\n- New `defcustom` `sp-writing-projects` in `sp-globals.el`, default `~/Documents/writing/` (below `sp-documents-dir`).\n- `vulpea-db-sync-directories` (`sp-vulpea-base.el`) is now `sp-notes-dir`, `user-emacs-directory` and `sp-writing-projects`.\n  - Folders that do not exist are left out, so a missing `~/Documents/writing/` does not break the scan.\n- Docs updated to match: `sp-globals.org` and `sp-vulpea.org` (\"Synced directories\").\n\n## How the headings and IDs get in\n- IDs: Vulpea indexes the `:ID:` entries of everything in `vulpea-db-sync-directories`.\n- TODO headings: `vulpea-para` tags a file for the agenda on save when it holds an open TODO (any `org-todo-keywords` keyword). Its scope is `vulpea-db-sync-directories`, so the writing folder is covered.\n- Files that already have open TODOs need `M-x vulpea-para-agenda-backfill` once, and `M-x vulpea-db-sync-full-scan` (or a restart) indexes the new folders.\n\n## Not verified\n- Not run in Emacs (none in the cloud container).\n- The config directory is now indexed, so its Org docs with TODO headings also join the agenda once saved.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCtkuUzuiths11Hu1j)_",
